// rk_thememenu_shim.jsfx-inc — the things rk_swing_popup needs from Swing
//
// ⚠️⚠️ rk_swing_popup.jsfx-inc looks self-contained (it has no imports of its own
// and reads only mouse globals) but it CALLS helpers it does not define:
//     swing_px(px)   swing_fs(px)   swing_txt_wt(fs, s) (the headers)
// All three live in rk_swing_core.jsfx-inc; swing_px and swing_fs read the global
// _ui_sc. rk_swing_core is Swing's engine — thousands of lines and its own world
// — so a small face that only wants the popup widget must not drag it in. These
// three functions are the whole dependency, copied verbatim from rk_swing_core.
//
// Imported by the faces that use the popup without rk_swing_core: Steppa
// (EON_StepSeq), EON_Output and EON_Tone.
// ⛔ Do NOT import this into Swing (or anything that imports rk_swing_core): it
// already has the real definitions, and a second definition of the same
// function name is a redefinition, not an override.
//
// _ui_sc is Swing's global UI scale, used there to grow type with the window.
// A face with its own `sc` leaves this at 1 and scales its own drawing; the
// popup then measures in real pixels, which is what these faces want — their
// menus are small and fixed, not part of a scalable big view.

@init

_ui_sc = 1;
function swing_fs(px) ( max(6, floor(px * _ui_sc + 0.5)); );
function swing_px(px) ( floor(px * _ui_sc + 0.5); );
// Also from rk_swing_core, verbatim: the popup's headers call it (wiki 4.7).
function swing_txt_wt(fs, s) local(i, c, dig) (
  dig = 0;
  fs < 10 ? (
    i = 0;
    loop(strlen(s),
      c = str_getchar(s, i);
      (c >= '0' && c <= '9') ? ( dig = 1; );
      i += 1;
    );
  );
  dig ? 0 : 'b';
);
